This guide explains how to connect a GOTEK to a Compaq Portable II machine to run diagnostic software without needing to obtain disks/diskette drives.
Do not use this guide for a permanent installation; it is for temporary use only.

NEEDED ITEMS:
GOTEK Floppy Emulator
A standard 34-pin ribbon cable (Twisted)
3 male-female jumper wires
A power source capable of providing 5VDC (My setup uses an off-brand Arduino's power rail fed by a small battery pack, see image.)
USB flash drive

1. If not already done, flash your GOTEK Floppy Emulator with FlashFloppy; guides to this process can be found online.
2. Connect a jumper wire to the GOTEK's far power connector labeled in silkscreen "5V" and connect to your 5V power supply.
3. Connect the other two jumper wires to the GOTEK's middle power connectors labeled in silkscreen as "GND", and connect to the ground on your 5V power supply.
4. Connect the twisted end of the 34-pin ribbon cable to the GOTEK.
5. Configure the GOTEK jumpers to only MO and S1 on.
6. Open your Compaq and expose the drive controller card.
7. Unplug the cable connected to the drive controller card's port labeled "FLPY" on the silkscreen.
8. Install the non-twisted end of the GOTEK's 34-pin cable into the FLPY port.

Your setup is now ready for use.
